  {
   "id": "e186",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1440,
   "y": 452,
   "width": 343.20000000000005,
   "height": 406.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 185567036,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1024075532,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "• Match pins by the name printed on each board.\n  The order here keeps the wires straight.\n• Mic on 3V3 only (max 3.63 V). 5V destroys it.\n• Every LED has its own resistor. Two LEDs on\n  one resistor never light evenly.\n• LED long leg (anode) to the resistor; short\n  leg, flat side (cathode) to GND.\n• Diffused 3 mm LEDs, not clear ones.\n• Start at 100 Ω and look through the printed\n  panel: 47 Ω brighter, 220 Ω dimmer. Keep D7\n  (two LEDs) under 20 mA in total.\n• Check battery polarity with a multimeter\n  before soldering; mark the + wire with tape.\n• The switch cuts BAT+, so the battery charges\n  over USB-C only with the switch ON.\n• A short flicker of the trachea LED at power-on\n  is normal: D6 also carries the boot messages.\n• L/R to GND = left channel, as the firmware\n  reads it.\n• Arduino IDE: keep USB CDC On Boot = Enabled.\n  D6/D7 are also the serial pins.\n• Charging runs at 100 mA: an empty battery\n  needs about a day (switch ON, USB in).\n• Every ground symbol (three bars) is GND;\n  they are all joined together.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "• Match pins by the name printed on each board.\n  The order here keeps the wires straight.\n• Mic on 3V3 only (max 3.63 V). 5V destroys it.\n• Every LED has its own resistor. Two LEDs on\n  one resistor never light evenly.\n• LED long leg (anode) to the resistor; short\n  leg, flat side (cathode) to GND.\n• Diffused 3 mm LEDs, not clear ones.\n• Start at 100 Ω and look through the printed\n  panel: 47 Ω brighter, 220 Ω dimmer. Keep D7\n  (two LEDs) under 20 mA in total.\n• Check battery polarity with a multimeter\n  before soldering; mark the + wire with tape.\n• The switch cuts BAT+, so the battery charges\n  over USB-C only with the switch ON.\n• A short flicker of the trachea LED at power-on\n  is normal: D6 also carries the boot messages.\n• L/R to GND = left channel, as the firmware\n  reads it.\n• Arduino IDE: keep USB CDC On Boot = Enabled.\n  D6/D7 are also the serial pins.\n• Charging runs at 100 mA: an empty battery\n  needs about a day (switch ON, USB in).\n• Every ground symbol (three bars) is GND;\n  they are all joined together.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  }
 ],
